.SS "char * wget_strmemdup (const void * m, size_t n)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIm\fP Memory to convert into string 
.br
\fIn\fP Length of memory 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Created string
.RE
.PP
Convert the given memory region \fRm\fP with length \fRn\fP into a C string\&. Returns NULL if \fRm\fP is NULL\&.

.PP
You should free() the returned string when not needed any more\&. 
.SS "size_t wget_strmemcpy (char * s, size_t ssize, const void * m, size_t n)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIs\fP Buffer to hold the C string output 
.br
\fIssize\fP Size of the output buffer 
.br
\fIm\fP Memory to read from 
.br
\fIn\fP Length of memory 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Number of bytes copied, not counting the trailing 0 byte
.RE
.PP
Convert the given memory region \fRm\fP with length \fRn\fP into a C string at \fRs\fP\&. A max\&. of \fRssize\fP - 1 is copied into \fRs\fP\&. 
.SS "void * wget_strmemcpy_a (char * s, size_t ssize, const void * m, size_t n)"

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIs\fP Buffer to hold the C string output 
.br
\fIssize\fP Size of the output buffer 
.br
\fIm\fP Memory to read from 
.br
\fIn\fP Length of memory 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Pointer to destination (either \fRs\fP or a freshly allocated buffer)
.RE
.PP
Convert the given memory region \fRm\fP with length \fRn\fP into a C string at \fRs\fP or at freshly allocated memory, if the space in \fRs\fP was not sufficient\&.

.PP
If \fRs\fP was too small to hold \fRn\fP + 1 bytes, the result must be free'd after use, e\&.g\&. if (res != s) wget_free(res); 
